/-!
# The invariant inner projection in the component reduction

Universal 15.3.49(j) and `θ(M ∩ H) = Y₀` control invariant solvable subgroups
of the actual quotient `H/O₂(H)`. Cauchy's theorem lifts their order-three
subgroups through the two-group kernel. For an inner action on the
centerless component closure, uniqueness constructs the inner projection
and proves its invariance; commutator generation makes it nontrivial.
Its image is generated by elements of order three, so the solvable-overgroup
argument forces an order-three element into both component and `Y₀` images.
The source condition `|Y₀/O₂(Y₀)| = 3` and two-perfectness then lift the
containment to `Y₀ ≤ L₀`. No assumption that `|Y₀*| = 3` is made.

The last theorem supplies this terminal step for the legitimate replacement
`H = ⟨L^T⟩Y₀T`, deriving its normality and commutator identity. The preceding
Borel and outer-automorphism analysis must still prove the centerless inner
action hypotheses; this module does not assert the complete source (k).

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), proof of
15.3.49(k), printed p.1144.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Subgroup
open scoped IsMulCommutative
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.FusionCore.ExtraspecialElimination

